    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40010": {
      "title": "Administrative Analyst",
      "description": "Department: School of Nursing\nAdministrative Analyst | Working Title | Administrative Analyst | Position # | A01001 | Department | School of Nursing\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Administrative Analyst Working Title Administrative Analyst Position # A01001 Department School of Nursing Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $33,696.00 Closing: 11/2/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Administrative Analyst is responsible for conducting special research studies, analyzing data, preparing statistics, making recommendations based on research findings, and monitoring and coordinating project/program activities. Duties & Responsibilities: Report course/student progress and issues to the appropriate clinical coordinator Oversees collection and storage of required clinical documentation and student/preceptor demographic data Ensures clinical coverage Review clinical course offerings, verify sections, enrollment cap, dates/times, and appropriate faculty with registration personnel Assist clinical coordinator(s) in clinical courses within the options along with orienting, training, and assisting in problem-solving issues Coordinates utilization of clinical facilities and oversees maintenance of appropriate documentation (i.e. facilitators and clinical agency contracts) Assists with clinical placement of students Disseminates clinical site evaluation surveys to students as necessary Assist in coordinating clinical orientations with students, clinical faculty, and clinical facility liaisons Initiates and deploys ‘Welcome Letter’ and ‘Thank you Letter’ to clinical preceptors Communicates and maintains rapport with clinical site liaisons Assist in building clinical placement grids and maintaining current clinical placement grids Process clinical placement documentation and initiate clinical affiliation agreements Deploy clinical evaluations as scheduled Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of planning, research, and analysis techniques and procedures. Knowledge of department operations, policies, and procedures. Knowledge of applicable laws and regulations. Knowledge of basic accounting principles. Ability to plan and execute systems and organizational analysis and feasibility studies. Ability to conduct research and perform quantitative quality assurance reviews. Ability to research, prepare, and present comprehensive written and oral reports. Ability to organize and conduct meetings and workshops. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a bachelor’s degree in public administration, general business, or a related field. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
