    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40015": {
      "title": "Faculty 12 Mo",
      "description": "Department: College of Veterinary Medicine\nFaculty 12 Mo | Working Title | Associate or Full Professor | Position # | F00729 | Department | College of Veterinary Medicine\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Faculty 12 Mo Working Title Associate or Full Professor Position # F00729 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/23/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a 12-month, tenured faculty position at the Associate or Full Professor level in livestock, poultry, or aquaculture food safety, foodborne pathogens, and/or antimicrobial resistance. This predominantly research-focused position includes approximately 75% research, 15–20% teaching, and 5–10% service. The successful candidate will join the College’s emerging Food Animal Health and Production Initiative, with the opportunity to build a nationally recognized research program while complementing and expanding existing strengths in food animal health, poultry health, infectious disease, and antimicrobial resistance. As part of our emerging Food Animal Health and Production Initiative, we aim to advance food animal health and production through research excellence, innovation, and collaboration. In partnership with the Arkansas Research Alliance, we seek to translate discovery into solutions that improve animal health, strengthen agricultural productivity, and drive economic impact. Our vision is to establish Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine as a nationally recognized leader in food animal health and production research. Duties & Responsibilities: Develop an independent, extramurally funded research program Collaborate with existing A-State faculty and other faculty and staff across other agencies and organizations in Arkansas to create a nationally recognized food animal health research center of excellence Develop commercial applications for research findings Mentor and teach MS and PhD students, and postdoctoral researchers in molecular biosciences or related fields Teach in the foundational and/or clinical sciences curriculum of the DVM program Mentor and advise DVM students, graduate students, and postdoctoral trainees in scientific investigation Contribute to college and university committees and serve on regional or national professional organizations Other duties as assigned College Overview: The Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine is a newly established college located in one of the nation’s most important agricultural regions, creating exceptional opportunities for discovery and impact. The College is building research strengths in infectious disease, microbiology, pathology, and animal health and production, supported by strong connections with industry, producers, and academic partners. In partnership with the Arkansas Research Alliance, we are seeking to build transformative research programs and establish the state of Arkansas as a destination for excellence in food animal health and production. Required Documents: ·Cover letter that includes a statement of research experience and plans, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information of three references Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: · Demonstrated success in obtaining extramural funding (e.g., USDA, NIH, NSF, Foundation for Food and Agriculture Research) · Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff · Ability to communicate effectively across stakeholders · Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently · Experience translating research findings into intellectual property (preferred) General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date. The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Minimum Qualifications: · PhD · Five years of faculty experience · DVM or equivalent (preferred) · Board certification (e.g., LAIM, ACPV, ACVM, ACVCP) (preferred) E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40040": {
      "title": "Telecommunications Specialist",
      "description": "Department: Information and Technology Services\nTelecommunications Specialist | Working Title | Audio Visual Specialist (A/V & Classroom Technologies) | Position # | A02626 | Department | Information and Technology Services\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Telecommunications Specialist Working Title Audio Visual Specialist (A/V & Classroom Technologies) Position # A02626 Department Information and Technology Services Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $36,500.00 Closing: 11/7/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The department of Information and Technology Services are seeking and individual who can install, diagnose, service, and operate audio-visual equipment, as well as provide superior customer service. All applicants need to be able to work independently or as part of a team to achieve these tasks. Duties & Responsibilities: Focuses on daily operations, service calls, and project completion for the A/V & Classroom Technologies Services division Works as a liaison between 3 rd party vendors and the customer for the division Assists in inventory control and order processing for the division Assesses daily work and effectively prioritizes time efficiently. Assists with customer service improvement measures Completes work orders/service tickets for the division Works with the Business Technology Services division manager on billing and purchasing needs Evaluates the division's performance and identifies areas of improvement Assists in technical troubleshooting and problem remediation Assesses user needs and determines the best strategies to meet those needs Performs other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Excellent knowledge of management best practices and strong managerial skills • Solid communication and teamwork skills • Good conflict resolution and problem-solving skills • Excellent organizational and project management skills • The ability to navigate stressful work situations • Knowledge of the telecommunications industry, standards, and new technologies • Knowledge of quality customer service and service management strategies • Knowledge of how to create, manage, and modify budgets • Knowledge of effective project management practices • Ability to balance heavy workloads and delegate tasks as needs dictate • Ability to communicate complex designs/details effectively • Ability to lead a team of technical employees, focusing on teamwork, customer service, efficiency, and meeting user needs General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Ability to work off ladders and scaffolding, lift 50lbs, and work overhead and in tight spaces Maintain professional work appearance and outstanding customer interaction Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of an earned Associate's Degree in computer science, computer applications, mathematics, or a related field OR Two (2) years of experience in audio visual support Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
