    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39945": {
      "title": "Department Chairperson",
      "description": "Department: Psychology & Counseling\nDepartment Chairperson | Working Title | Department Chair of Psychology & Counseling | Position # | F00019 | Department | Psychology & Counseling\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Department Chairperson Working Title Department Chair of Psychology & Counseling Position # F00019 Department Psychology & Counseling Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/6/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department Chair is responsible to their respective Dean for the general management and operation of their academic areas. The Chair represents their department(s) to the dean and university administrators, supports faculty in their professional development, and works with faculty to improve instructional programs and to develop programs that are responsive to changing needs of students. Duties & Responsibilities: Represents their department(s) to the dean and university administrators Supports faculty in their professional development Works with faculty to improve instructional programs Works with program coordinators in Psychology (BS & BA), School Psychology, Clinical Mental Health Counseling, and School Counseling to understand the needs and support the goals of each program. Works with and supports in recruitment and retention of faculty Works with faculty to develop programs that are responsive to changing needs of students. Supervises faculty, conducts annual evaluations, and recommends tenured and nontenured faculty members to the dean of their college for employment, retention, promotion, tenure, non-renewal, and dismissal For the preparation and administration of budgets for the departments; Evaluates and recommends program offerings to the dean For the supervision of the academic mentoring of students majoring in the department Responsible for the acquisition, use, and care of departmental equipment. Addresses student concerns and academic appeals/grievances Acts as a liaison between faculty and administrators Ensures compliance with university policies Ensures accreditation standards are maintained Promotes the department’s accomplishments and impact Encourages and sustains scholarship, research, and participation in professional activities by members of their faculty Maintains an active program of scholarship appropriate to the discipline Works with and assists in recruitment and retention of students Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Ability to work collaboratively with program coordinators and faculty across the department's research and professional programs, including supporting accreditation processes for the counseling and school psychology programs (CACREP, NASP). General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance 12-month contract Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date. Preferred Qualifications: Prior academic leadership experience, such as serving as a program coordinator or director. Experience with program accreditation, program review, or assessment is also valued. Minimum Qualifications: Doctorate in psychology, counseling, or a closely related field. Candidates must have a record of teaching, scholarship, and service that meets the Department of Psychology & Counseling's Promotion, Retention, and Tenure (PRT) criteria for appointment with tenure at the rank of associate or full professor. Must be eligible for graduate faculty status at Arkansas State University. Required Documentation: Cover letter, application, resume, 2 letters of recommendation, 3 reference names other than recommenders, and transcripts. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39868": {
      "title": "Department Chairperson",
      "description": "Department: History\nDepartment Chairperson | Working Title | Department Chairperson | Position # | F00005 | Department | History\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Department Chairperson Working Title Department Chairperson Position # F00005 Department History Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 12/21/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department Chair needs to be motivating, organized, and supportive. The Chair leads and manages departmental faculty and staff. They are responsible to their respective Dean for the general management and operation of their academic areas. The Chair represents the department to the Dean and university administrators, supports faculty in their scholarship and professional development, and works with faculty to improve instructional programs and to develop programs that are responsive to the changing needs of students. Some administrative experience at Chair, Assistant Chair, or Program Director is preferred, though applicants meeting minimum qualifications will be considered. Duties & Responsibilities: Evaluating and recommending faculty members to the Dean of their college for employment, retention, promotion, tenure, non-renewal, and dismissal Encouraging and sustaining scholarship, research, grant activity and participation in professional activities by members of faculty in alignment with A-State’s R2 status. Supervising other personnel in the department Preparing and administrating departmental budgets Coordinating curricular development; strategic planning; outreach and recruitment; alumni audience and donor relations; and service activities while demonstrating commitment to excellence in teaching The standard teaching load for department chairs is two courses per academic semester Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Arkansas State University is a comprehensive R2 public university located along Crowley’s Ridge approximately 70 miles northwest of Memphis. The History department offers a well-rounded curriculum through the BA in History and the BSE in Social Science, and also offers courses in Geography. The department offers the MA in History on campus and online. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in History. A tenured appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor Required Documentation: CV, cover letter, and a list of 3 - 5 references E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39909": {
      "title": "Project Program Director",
      "description": "Department: Fowler Center\nProject Program Director | Working Title | Director of Fowler Center | Position # | A02710 | Department | Fowler Center\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Project Program Director Working Title Director of Fowler Center Position # A02710 Department Fowler Center Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/31/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University invites nominations and applications for the position of Director of Fowler Center. Fowler Center stands at the center of artistic life at Arkansas State University. Serving students, faculty, artists, and the surrounding region, the center houses theatre productions, concerts, museum exhibitions, guest artists, educational programs, conferences, and community events throughout the year. As the home of the Bradbury Art Museum and multiple performance venues, Fowler Center unites visual art, music, theatre, and public engagement under one roof. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Liberal Arts and Communication, the Director is responsible for all aspects of building operations and management including event booking, box office, scheduling, staffing, equipment, and property. The Director will have a thorough knowledge and understanding of concepts, principles, and practices of event management; a proven record of booking musical and entertainment talent and academic lectures; and, strong marketing and promotion experience with similar type venues to facilitate fulfillment of A-State’s vision for Fowler Center to be recognized as a premier arts and cultural event center. Duties & Responsibilities: Direct management of all academic and public-facing spaces in Fowler Direct booking of top musical and entertainment talent and academic presentations across a variety of venues Direct marketing initiatives for all events in Fowler Direct staff to provide exceptional customer service for each event Oversee financial management of Fowler by preparing a budget based on goals and monitoring expenditures with financial records. Lead recruitment of all staff positions, including full-time, part-time, and student employment Monitor industry trends and news that will have a local impact on the organization Coordinate with the Department of Theatre, Department of Music, and the Bradbury Art Museum for Fowler scheduling and promotional needs as appropriate Conduct key constituent meetings Promote a facility reputation for outstanding customer service Develop a year-round facility maintenance plan, including discussion of long-term improvements and short-term maintenance, working with Facilities Management to define scope of work and cost estimates. Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of concepts, principles and practices of event management Proven record of effective management of a facility comparable to Fowler Center Strong marketing and promotion experience with similar-type venues and a proven track record of growing business and enhancing customer experience Excellent people management skills General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance This position requires the flexibility to work various hours based upon need and may include days, nights, weekends, and holidays Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: An earned Bachelor’s Degree with an emphasis in Fine Arts, marketing, event management, management, or a related field Senior-level arena or venue management, substantial marketing, or management job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for education E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39992": {
      "title": "Fiscal Support Supervisor",
      "description": "Department: Dean of Liberal Arts\nFiscal Support Supervisor | Working Title | Fiscal Support Supervisor | Position # | A00766 | Department | Dean of Liberal Arts\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Fiscal Support Supervisor Working Title Fiscal Support Supervisor Position # A00766 Department Dean of Liberal Arts Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $40,000.00 Closing: 11/26/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Fiscal Support Supervisor is responsible for supervising the activities of fiscal support personnel within an assigned department or program. This position is governed by Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), state and federal laws and institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Fiscal support supervisor responsible for all budget and accounting issues across all departments in the college; reviews, verifies, and approves all budget related documents submitted to the budget office Maintains faculty and staff computer inventory Works with three ITS staff assigned to CLAC to collect quotes for purchasing computers Supports ITS staff with maintaining classroom inventory records; initiates process for purchasing computers for all computer labs and classrooms in HSS, Fine Arts, ED/COMM, Fowler, Art Annex Supports all units with Taleo Reviews and verifies all Extra Compensation Forms and EPAFs Facilitates allocation of professional development funds Oversees all Foundation Accounts Prepares budget spreadsheet for graduate assistants for the college Facilitates expenditures of academic capital funds Provides support for departments with AOS revenue sharing accounts Provides budget support and performs other selected fiscal processing duties to support Printing Services Develops reports requested by AAR for the college: Auxiliary/Special Funding Budgets Infrastructure Spending Report Merit Recommendations Summer Instruction requests Off-Budget requests Carry-forward Spending Plans Faculty Reassignment Report Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of staff development and supervision principles. Knowledge of department operations, policies and procedures, applicable laws and regulations. Knowledge of software application programs, database management, and accounting principles. Ability to conduct research and perform quantitative quality assurance reviews, resolve operational problems, and prepare required reports. Ability to plan, organize and coordinate activities, resources, and materials associated with the needs of the department or program. Ability to plan and direct the work of others. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a bachelor in general business, business administration, finance, or a related field. Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40033": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Department: Dean of Nursing and Health Prof\nAcademic Advisor | Working Title | Health Professions Academic Advisor | Position # | A00156 | Department | Dean of Nursing and Health Prof\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Academic Advisor Working Title Health Professions Academic Advisor Position # A00156 Department Dean of Nursing and Health Prof Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $45,000.00 Closing: 11/13/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Health Professions Academic Advisor informs and assists current students and prospective students. This includes pre-professional semester schedule planning and answering questions about the programs in the College of Nursing and Health Professions during advising or recruiting events. This position may require travel and periodic evening or weekend hours. Duties & Responsibilities: Provides academic advising to students in selected health professions by: Accurately advising students according to degree requirements Making sure Honors students have correct honors courses Is aware of: Scholarship requirements and advises accordingly International Program requirements and advises accordingly Workforce, TAA and VA requirements and advises accordingly S Schedules student advising in a timely fashion Facilitates documentation and record-keeping in advising-related software Promptly answers emails and phone calls in support of student appointments and questions. Maintains accurate student records Meets regularly with Program Directs and Chairs of the programs for which they advise to stay up-to-date with program information Maintains good rapport with students, other advisors, and Program Directors/Chairs Recruits and promotes Health Professions programs by participating in: Area career and academic fairs Recruitment events Honors College Days New Student Registration Days Corresponds with all student services areas across campus Participates in the assessment process when necessary May teach a Making Connections course as needed May serve on assigned program, college and university committees Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Must have working knowledge of requirements of various programs in the health professions. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance This position may require travel and periodic evening or weekend hours. Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: An earned Bachelor’s Degree E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40006": {
      "title": "Skilled Tradesman",
      "description": "Department: FM-Business Services\nSkilled Tradesman | Working Title | Lock Shop Technician | Position # | A00666 | Department | FM-Business Services\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Skilled Tradesman Working Title Lock Shop Technician Position # A00666 Department FM-Business Services Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $35,500.00 Closing: 10/31/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Skilled Tradesman is responsible for the work activities in one or more of the following skilled trades; HVAC (Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning), Plumbing, Electrical, Carpentry, and Mechanical, Lock and Security. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Maintain key and lock records Receive and process key requests Issue and receive keys Answer phones and assist customers Maintain key box records and access Complete workflows when employees terminate Back up University Locksmith as needed Assist in Warehouse as needed Assist with counting inventory for year-end audit Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of Microsoft Office, general computer skills, FAMIS experience a plus, or the ability to learn computer programs as needed Ability to communicate with a diverse customer base, good customer service skills, and have the ability to work with a diverse team General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 7:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date This position is considered Essential Personnel in Facilities Management Individuals who can operate/drive a vehicle with a manual transmission is preferred One (1) year of Locksmith or Key Cutting experience is preferred Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma plus 1 year of locksmith or key cutting experience Preferred to have a valid Driver's License E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
