    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=38795": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 12 Mo",
      "description": "Department: College of Veterinary Medicine\nAssistant Professor 12 Mo | Working Title | Assistant/Associate Professor of Small Animal Urgent Care | Position # | F00722 | Department | College of Veterinary Medicine\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 12 Mo Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Small Animal Urgent Care Position # F00722 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/20/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a clinical assistant or associate professor in Small Animal Urgent Care. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This position incorporates clinical work (24 weeks/year) with workplace-based year 4 student training in urgent care/emergency, teaching of year 1-3 students in clinical skills and urgent/emergency care. Service (10%) is also expected. Scholarly activity appointment is negotiable. Duties & Responsibilities: Teach year 1-3 DVM students the principles and practice of urgent care and emergency medicine in the classroom, clinical skills laboratory Teach year 4 DVM students urgent care and emergency medicine in clinical practice Provide excellent patient care and clinical service, including communication with clients and referring veterinarians Contribute to competency-based curriculum development with a focus on small animal emergency medicine and urgent care across years 1-4 of the DVM curriculum Contribute to objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs) and other skills-based assessments Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Mentor and advise DVM students +/- Contribute to scholarly endeavors through collaborative educational research and/or educational innovations Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff. • Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders. • Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently. General Days/Hours: Variable hours (approximately 4 pm-12 am when on clinical duty, M-Th, ~24 weeks per year; 8 am-5 pm M-F when not on clinic duty) Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Required Documents: Cover letter, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information of three references Minimum Qualifications: • DVM or equivalent • Board certification in a small animal specialty (preferred) (e.g., ACVECC) • Two (2) years of teaching experience (preferred) • Experience in competency-based veterinary education (preferred) E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39901": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 9 Mo",
      "description": "Department: School of Nursing\nAssistant Professor 9 Mo | Working Title | Assistant Professor of Nursing | Position # | F00259 | Department | School of Nursing\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Nursing Position # F00259 Department School of Nursing Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 12/4/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Nine (9)- month non-tenure-track undergraduate faculty position in the ACEN-accredited A-State School of Nursing. Participation in teaching and professional service is expected. This position is full-time, with a focus on weekend clinical placement in the BSN and AASN program options. Duties & Responsibilities: Actively participates in development and evaluation of curriculum, course content, clinical experiences, and test construction. Responsible for clinical and didactic courses appropriate to areas of expertise. Plans and supervises clinical seminars. Establishes effective coordinating relationships with co-workers and clinical agencies. Continues education for professional growth through continuing education offerings. Participates in student mentoring and guidance. Maintains regular office hours on campus and virtually Participates in appropriate program, college and university activities as assigned for faculty and/or student recruitment and retention Serves on assigned program, college, and university committees. Sponsors and promotes planned activities of students, program, college and university as requested. Contributes to the community through involvement in and/or consultation to health-related organizations, board memberships, or professional presentations to the public Holds membership and participates in organizations that advance the profession of nursing, such as ANA, ARNA, Sigma, or other professional organizations Optional Participation in nursing research and other scholarly work, including but not limited to presentations at professional meetings, publications, grant applications, book and textbook reviews, and enrollment in university courses. Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of curriculum design, strategies to promote student learning, assessment and evaluation of learning, evidence-based education principles, basic nursing skills and a commitment to life-long learning. Possesses interpersonal and communication skills necessary to teach as part of a faculty team. Knowledge, skills, and abilities required or applicable to the position responsibilities and area of specialization, including special abilities. General Days/Hours: Primarily weekend coverage, Typically, Thursday - Monday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. (hours vary related to clinical rotations, office hours, didactic course load, and other program activities). Regular and reliable attendance on campus and assigned clinical facility. Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Up to 15 credit hour teaching workload. Primary coverage is weekends for online program options for undergraduate nursing, assistance with covering on campus and distant campus program options, as needed Academic experience preferred in the areas of medical/surgical nursing, ICU, mental health, and/or maternal/child. A cover letter, resume, and a list of 3 references must be attached (in MS Word or PDF format) to the electronic application Minimum Qualifications: 1) An Earned Doctorate degree required, PhD preferred, or DNP 2) Unencumbered licensure to practice nursing as an RN in Arkansas or a compact state. 3) At least two (2) years of clinical practice as an RN. 4) Didactic and/or clinical teaching experience in nursing, preferred. *If the degree held is a Masters of Science in Nursing Degree, the position will be at the rank of Instructor. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39691": {
      "title": "Administrative Analyst",
      "description": "Department: Assoc CFO/CAO\nAdministrative Analyst | Working Title | Document Imaging Coordinator | Position # | A00951 | Department | Assoc CFO/CAO\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Administrative Analyst Working Title Document Imaging Coordinator Position # A00951 Department Assoc CFO/CAO Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $33,696.00 Closing: 11/12/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Administrative Analyst is responsible for conducting special research studies, analyzing data, preparing statistics, making recommendations based on research findings, and monitoring and coordinating project/program activities. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Gather appropriate documents for imaging Organize the documents into appropriate categories Scan and index the documents within the appropriate application Coordinate with ITS for troubleshooting issues and creating new applications Provide training and support for functional users Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of planning, research, and analysis techniques and procedures, department operations, policies, and procedures, applicable laws and regulations, and basic accounting principles Ability to plan and execute systems and organizational analysis and feasibility studies, conduct research and perform quantitative quality assurance reviews, research, prepare, and present comprehensive written and oral reports, and organize and conduct meetings and workshops General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of an earned Bachelor's Degree in public administration, general business, or a related field Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40055": {
      "title": "Institutional Services Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Student Union Building Maintenance\nInstitutional Services Assistant | Working Title | Institutional Services Assistant | Position # | A01216 | Department | Student Union Building Maintenance\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Institutional Services Assistant Working Title Institutional Services Assistant Position # A01216 Department Student Union Building Maintenance Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $27,040.00 Closing: 11/15/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Institutional Services Assistant is responsible for general cleaning of areas in and around office buildings, class rooms, lecture halls, conference rooms, auditoriums, resident halls, dining areas, building common areas, and other areas as required. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Empties waste baskets, dumps trash, and replaces trash bags. Wipes clean furniture such as desktops, tables, and other surfaces. Cleans floors by sweeping, vacuuming, and mopping as required. Cleans restroom facilities. Replaces paper towels and tissue as needed and maintains an adequate supply of each. Notifies supervisor of maintenance and repairs needed in areas cleaned. Assists in room and audiovisual set-ups. Ensures building security by watching for vandalism and patron safety. Performs minor repairs on building equipment and furnishings. Performs related responsibilities as required or assigned. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of basic cleaning techniques. Knowledge of cleaning equipment operation and maintenance. Ability to follow instructions and perform repetitive manual work. Ability to use cleansers and other agents to clean floors and furniture. Ability to use housekeeping cleaning supplies and equipment. Ability to work independently without close supervision. Ability to follow oral and/or written instructions. Ability to perform multiple tasks and to prioritize assignments. Ability to perform repetitive manual work. Ability to do required lifting (up to 50 lbs.). General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 6:00 am - 3:00 pm Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40053": {
      "title": "Institutional Services Supervisor",
      "description": "Department: Student Union Building Maintenance\nInstitutional Services Supervisor | Working Title | Institutional Services Supervisor | Position # | A01155 | Department | Student Union Building Maintenance\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Institutional Services Supervisor Working Title Institutional Services Supervisor Position # A01155 Department Student Union Building Maintenance Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $29,000.00 Closing: 11/17/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Institutional Services Supervisor is responsible for overseeing and monitoring custodial and minor maintenance activities in building facilities and supervising laundry room functions in an institutional setting. This position is governed by state and federal laws and institutional policy. Responsible for supervising some institutional services assistants, cleaning duties, and event setups (lifting tables and chairs). Duties & Responsibilities: Supervises a medium to large-sized custodial staff engaged in cleaning assigned areas Trains employees in methods and procedures for cleaning and maintaining proper standards Handles special cleaning assignments and emergency spills Orders and maintains inventory of cleaning supplies Performs routine inspections of buildings and work assigned to subordinate employees Coordinates maintenance and repair needs with the appropriate personnel Coordinates and assists in room and audiovisual set-ups Ensures building security by watching for vandalism and patron safety Performs minor repairs on building equipment and furnishings as needed Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of supervisory practices and procedures. Knowledge of custodial and maintenance practices and techniques. Knowledge of materials and equipment used in custodial and maintenance work. Knowledge of the operation and maintenance requirements of commercial laundry equipment. Ability to maintain adequate supplies and inventory records. Ability to prepare written documents. Ability to conduct inspections to determine compliance with standards. Ability to supervise staff of subordinate supervisors, custodial workers and semi-skilled maintenance repairmen. General Days/Hours: Tuesday - Sunday 6:00 AM to 3:00 PM Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date This position is considered Essential Personnel with Facilities Management Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma One (1) year of vocational training and/or experience in housekeeping Preferred to possess a valid Driver's License E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39066": {
      "title": "Instructor 12 Mo",
      "description": "Department: College of Veterinary Medicine\nInstructor 12 Mo | Working Title | Teaching Assistant or Associate Professor of Large Animal Ambulatory Practice | Position # | F00730 | Department | College of Veterinary Medicine\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Instructor 12 Mo Working Title Teaching Assistant or Associate Professor of Large Animal Ambulatory Practice Position # F00730 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 12/10/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a faculty position in Large Animal Veterinary Ambulatory Medicine and Surgery (Equine and Livestock). This will be a 12-month, full time, non-tenure track, Assistant or Associate Professor position. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This will be a predominantly clinical position (60-80% clinical service and clinical teaching), pre-clinical (years 1-3) teaching (10-30%), and service (10%). Promoting and providing large animal ambulatory veterinary services to the Jonesboro and surrounding local communities. Duties & Responsibilities: Promote the A-State Large Animal Ambulatory Service Provide day-time veterinary ambulatory care to large animal species including horses, donkeys, cattle, sheep, goats, and swine to the Jonesboro community, surrounding  communities, and any other stakeholders (8-a.m. to 5-p.m.)  (estimated 50% livestock and 50% equine patients) Provide emergency veterinary ambulatory care to established A-State Large Animal Ambulatory Veterinary service clients and A-State animals Lead and manage herd-health protocols for established ambulatory clients Work collaboratively with other A-State and local veterinarians and staff Manage ambulatory technician personnel Contribute to didactic and clinicals skills related education for DVM students Contribute to large animal IACUC protocols. Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff • Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders • Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. On-call afterhours care as needed to established clients and A-State animals Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Required documents: Cover letter, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information of three references Minimum Qualifications: • DVM or equivalent • Board certification in a large-animal specialty (e.g., ACVS-LA, ACVIM-LA) (preferred) E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40062": {
      "title": "Student Development Specialist",
      "description": "Department: Dean of Students-Educational Prgms\nStudent Development Specialist | Working Title | Coordinator of Operations | Position # | A00515 | Department | Dean of Students-Educational Prgms\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Student Development Specialist Working Title Coordinator of Operations Position # A00515 Department Dean of Students-Educational Prgms Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 12/16/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Coordinator of Operations is a full-time, 12-month, live-in position with oversight of occupancy management in a fast paced University Housing office. This reports directly to the Assistant Director of Operations. The Coordinator of Operations is highly focused and demonstrates an ability to provide a comprehensive team approach to customer service. Duties & Responsibilities: Oversee assignment coordination for campus residents Oversee meal plan assignments and pro-rations for on and off campus residents Manage day-to-day resolution of departmental issues related to the areas of responsibility Responsible for all areas related to student contracts, assignments, and housing database Coordinate departmental master operational calendar Assist with assignment logistics of summer camps and conferences Participate in short and long range planning with University Housing Leadership Team Perform other duties as assigned to support the mission of the University Housing department Other duties as assigned Under the Clery Act, Residence Life staff are considered Campus Security Authorities and as such are required by law to report the following crimes to the on-call system and to UPD immediately upon learning of them: criminal homicide, sex offenses, robbery, aggravated assault, burglary, motor vehicle theft, arson, liquor law violations, drug violations, weapons violations, stalking, domestic violence and dating violence. This position is also required to report bias-related (hate) crimes for the following offenses: criminal homicide, sex offenses, robbery, aggravated assault, burglary, motor vehicle theft, arson, larceny-theft, intimidation, simple assault and damage/destruction/vandalism of property Serve in a designated on-call rotation with other University Housing professional staff members being on call approximately 2-5 weeks throughout each semester, including summer and break periods Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of state, federal, and university policies, procedures and regulations regarding campus housing Strong oral and written communication skills, critical thinking skills, decision making skills, customer service oriented, understanding of student development theory, positive attitude General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: The Coordinator of Operations has daily contact with all department staff. Participation in local and state professional organizations is encouraged. Travel to conference training sessions is required Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) or more years of Residence Life management experience An earned Master's Degree in College Student Personnel or related field Minimum Qualifications: An earned Bachelor's Degree in a related field E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40049": {
      "title": "Curator",
      "description": "Department: Museum\nCurator | Working Title | Curator of Education | Position # | A00899 | Department | Museum\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Curator Working Title Curator of Education Position # A00899 Department Museum Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/25/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Curator is responsible for guiding the museum’s educational initiatives including tours (K-12, university students, adults), events, classes, etc. within a cooperative and collaborative team atmosphere. This position supports the museum within its parent organization and provides a bridge for the campus to diverse audiences; it helps translate collections, exhibits, and scholarship into learning experiences. Duties are often completed with considerable independence under the general supervision of the Museum Director/Curator of Collections, and alongside the Curator of Exhibitions. The Curator of Education will be a member of the Curatorial Committee, the group that guides critical museum decisions and functions, including strategic program, exhibition, and collections development. The position also may meet regularly with members of the Museum Advisory Council, a volunteer group dedicated to supporting the museum and its mission. Arkansas State University Museum, an AAM accredited museum, serves the academic mission of the university and provides quality programming to the people of Northeast Arkansas and the Northern Mississippi River Delta region. The Curator of Education is a full-time, 40-hour-per-week staff position. Duties & Responsibilities: Lead in the creation, implementation, and evaluation of all the museum’s informal education programs, including tours, traveling suitcase exhibits (TSEs), special classes, events, etc. Ensure that programs complement the mission, exhibits, and collections of the museum; suit various learning levels and styles Lead K-12 tours that are linked to state curriculum. Liaise with schools, co-ops, scouts, adults or other groups to schedule tours, programs, or events; ensure relevancy of the museum programs to client needs. Plan and deliver K-12 teacher professional development when requested. Interact with university faculty and staff to: promote student visitorship, develop programs/tours intersecting with campus curriculum, and work directly with graduate and undergraduate students. Serve as needed on university-wide initiatives and work in collaboration with other museums governed by the university. Works in collaboration with the Director and members of the Museum Advisory Council. Schedules and manages work-study students and volunteers. Develop and coordinate media/press releases related to the museums’ programs, events and exhibitions (with director and university communications office approval); appear on various media outlets promoting museum activities. Serves as a key player in museum’s long-range planning, grant writing, exhibition development, etc. Develop and implement methods to evaluate educational programming, including visitor participation, learning outcomes, accessibility, audience satisfaction, and community engagement. Use assessment findings to inform future programming and support the museum’s strategic planning and accreditation responsibilities. The above description and qualifications are not all-inclusive and represent the majority of key responsibilities for this position. Additional collaborative responsibilities assigned as needed Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: · Work experience in museums or other informal education environments; skills in interpretation and object-based learning practices. · Familiarity with accessibility, cultural competency, and inclusive interpretive practices. · Work experience in university/college museums or small museum settings is a plus. · Candidates should be creative and budget-minded. · Work environment is a combination of office setting and exhibition floor; periods of extensive physical activity are expected as exhibition/education space is spread out over two floors of galleries. · Ability to work occasional evenings or weekends may be required to fulfill program requirements. · Strong working knowledge of museum best practices in museum education. · Excellent written and verbal communication, interpersonal, and presentation skills are required, as this position works with other museum staff, university faculty, on-campus and off-campus collaborators, media, and provides mentorship opportunities for students. · This position is governed by state and federal laws and institutional policies. General Days/Hours: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM Ability to work occasional evenings or weekends may be required to fulfill program requirements Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree preferred in Museum Studies, History, Art History, Education, Anthropology or a closely related field. 3-5 years of experience preferred, emphasizing education in informal learning environments. Minimum Qualifications: A minimum of a Bachelor’s degree in Museum Studies, History, Art History, Education, Anthropology, or a closely related field, plus additional years of training or experience. Submitted material should include a letter of interest, resumé, teaching statement regarding education in an informal learning environment, and 3-4 references with complete information. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40044": {
      "title": "Temporary Assistant Professor 12 Mo",
      "description": "Department: Leadership and Special Education\nTemporary Assistant Professor 12 Mo | Working Title | Temporary Assistant Professor in Higher Ed Leadership | Position # | F00064 | Department | Leadership and Special Education\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Temporary Assistant Professor 12 Mo Working Title Temporary Assistant Professor in Higher Ed Leadership Position # F00064 Department Leadership and Special Education Apply Now Employment Status: Temporary (1 Year Assignment) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Telecommute - Jonesboro Campus Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/25/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Educational Leadership, Curriculum and Special Education (ELCSE) in the College of Education and Behavioral Science at Arkansas State University offers a fully online Doctor of Education (Ed.D.) in Educational Leadership, housed in the Center for Excellence in Education. The program has a P-12 track and a Higher Education Leadership track. It serves practitioner-scholars, most of whom work full-time as leaders in schools, colleges, and universities. Our program is a member of the Carnegie Project on the Education Doctorate (CPED). Students complete a dissertation focused on real problems in their own organizations. The department also offers master’s, specialist, and graduate certificate programs in educational leadership and related fields. Applicants are invited to apply for a 12-month, non-tenure-track Assistant Professor position with an anticipated start date of January 4, 2027. We're looking for a higher education scholar-practitioner who has real-world leadership experience and a strong grounding in applied research methods. This faculty member will teach doctoral courses, chair and serve on dissertation committees, and help students design rigorous, ethical, practical research that improves their institutions. Candidates will teach in the Doctoral Program in Higher Education Leadership, which is a fully online program. The successful candidate will be a strong collaborator and have a desire to connect with colleagues and build relationships to ensure a strong program. The ideal candidate will have experience developing and teaching doctoral-level courses, chairing and serving on dissertation committees, advising and mentoring program students, and being involved in appropriate activities for the maintenance and continuous improvement of the program, particularly as our program aligns with its membership in the Carnegie Project on the Education Doctorate (CPED). Candidates are expected to be well-versed in research methods, higher education leadership practices, policy and law, finance, and research. We’re looking for someone who brings a positive, solutions-focused, “let’s figure it out” approach and communicates promptly and openly with colleagues and students. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching Develop and teach online doctoral courses for practitioner-scholars in Canvas, including courses in higher education leadership and applied research methods Facilitate engaging, high-quality online learning experiences aligned with college and university distance education standards Provide timely, substantive, and constructive feedback on student work Maintain a consistent, visible presence in asynchronous and synchronous course environments Dissertation Support and Advising Chair and serve on dissertation committees Collaborate with committee members to support steady student progress Advise and mentor doctoral students Support ethical and rigorous research practices, including IRB and data integrity standards Program Service Work collaboratively with faculty in the Ed.D. and other department programs Participate in virtual program, department, and college faculty meetings Contribute to program initiatives, including curriculum development, assessment and continuous improvement aligned with CPED principles Maintain Graduate Faculty status in accordance with university policy Other duties as assigned Technology and Remote Work Expectations Deliver instruction and communication via Canvas and Microsoft Teams Maintain regular virtual presence Adhere to FERPA and data security policies Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Expertise in higher education leadership, including areas such as policy, law, finance and organizational practice • Strong background in research methods (quantitative, qualitative and/or mixed methods), especially applied and practitioner-oriented research • Ability to explain complex concepts clearly to adult learners • Experience supporting diverse graduate students in online environments • Commitment to the learning and development needs of students earning their degrees at a distance • Ability to guide and supervise graduate-level student research General Days/Hours: Primarily Monday- Friday, 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM Central Time, with additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Faculty are expected to provide timely feedback (typically within 24 hours), maintain availability for doctoral students, and support a flexible schedule including evening or limited weekend engagement. This position has been identified as a telecommuting position.  The duties are performed during standard work hours of 8am-5pm at a predefined and approved work location.  Individuals filling this role must have dedicated work space that provides privacy and security related to the work being performed.  Additionally, individuals must have secure internet access with appropriate upload/download capabilities to perform the duties associated with the position.  Individuals in this position will be required to review and acknowledge the Telecommuting Guidelines and Telecommuting Agreement for A-State. Location Requirement:  To be considered for this position, candidates must reside in Arkansas or a state that shares a border with Arkansas (Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Missouri, or Oklahoma.  This residency requirement supports team collaboration, regional knowledge, and occasional in-person engagement as needed. Please attach the following to your application: · Application letter · Curriculum vitae · Copy of graduate transcripts · Professional references This position emphasizes teaching and doctoral support. There are no formal research publication requirements; however, scholarly engagement is encouraged where appropriate and required to obtain/maintain Graduate Faculty Status. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree from an accredited university with a focus on Higher Education Administration or a related field Preferred Qualifications: • Professional leadership experience in higher education (e.g., student affairs, academic affairs, enrollment management, finance or institutional research) • Experience teaching graduate-level courses, particularly online • Experience chairing and/or serving on dissertation committees • Familiarity with Ed.D. programs, CPED principles, the Dissertation in Practice or improvement science • Experience teaching or designing courses in Canvas E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    }
  },
